## Expected breakage

Existing test classes (not this ticket's story tests) that the stubs will make fail without the stub in the failure or its root cause, for example a CLI or end-to-end test that reduces the stub to an exit code, a FAILED status or an empty result. One bullet per class, `` - `<SimpleClassName>`: <one-line reason> ``, with the class's simple name only (no package). The red gate reads only bullets under this exact heading and accepts every failure in a declared class; each of those tests must still pass at `green`. A test that fails directly on this ticket's stub needs no entry. "None." if no such class exists.

